Subject: [PATCH 3/5] CM-C+ D=4 correctness battery: 48/48 pass vs the trusted
 CM reference path

overnight_cm_cplus_d4_gate.jl exercises the REAL production wiring (cm_production_gradient vs
cm_production_gradient_cplus, both off build_cm_production_context/archC_base_state) at
D=4/L=10, both contrasts (:anchored, :orthonormal), 3 points (calibration + two perturbation
scales chosen to exercise different winner configurations):

  Section 1: base-point q0 agreement (CM-Reference builder vs CM-C+ builder) -- max diff
             5.7e-14 to 8.9e-16 (machine precision).
  Section 2: full production-wiring gradient agreement at matched h=0.01 -- max|dg| 1.4e-15 to
             2.0e-13, cosine 1.0 to 1e-10, zero A-block sign mismatches, across all 3 points x
             2 contrast bases (PRIMARY gate, per the task brief -- CM-C+ must agree with
             CM-reference, not merely with unrestricted C+).
  Section 3: independent bandwidth bisections (select_bandwidth vs select_bandwidth_C, each
             backend choosing its own h) still agree to cosine 1.0 - 5e-14.
  Section 4: fixed-dual secant (Reference) == fixed-dual secant (C+) exactly, both differing
             from the true reoptimized central-FD secant by the SAME known AUD-05 approximation
             gap (shared, not a C+-specific error) -- the two gates (2.3 vs 2.4 in the task
             brief) are kept separate, not conflated.

48/48 checks pass. One pre-existing gotcha found and documented inline: build_lfix_base_cache_C!'s
own validate_dense=true self-check is incompatible with a CM-augmented ctx (compares against the
FULL obj.moments! dot product over 1:oci-1, which includes the CM tail columns q0 intentionally
omits pre-correction) -- same reason the existing Reference CM test
(c13_validate_cm_aware_lfix.jl) never passes validate_dense=true against ctx_cm either. Not a bug
in this session's new code; documented so a future caller doesn't rediscover it the hard way.
